[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Intertube.Stub SMTP server requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: intertube.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document specifies the ready-made SMTP server in the ``Intertube.Stub.Smtp`` namespace: ``SmtpServer`` and its options (``SmtpServerOptions``), the per-connection SMTP session (RFC 5321, with STARTTLS per RFC 3207 and AUTH PLAIN/LOGIN per RFC 4954), its fault injection and interception hooks, and the captured ``SmtpMessage`` with its light MIME reading (RFC 2045, 2046 and 2047). Requirements with UIDs ``ITS-SMTP-*`` cover the protocol and server; ``ITS-MIME-*`` cover the parsing of captured messages. The underlying TCP server, connections, TLS and transcripts are specified elsewhere and are referenced here only where the SMTP server depends on them.

The key words "shall", "should" and "may" carry the meaning given in RFC 2119.

VERIFIED_BY lists the automated tests that exercise each requirement, as ``TypeName.MemberName``: the C# test class and method, or for F# the module name and the test's double-backticked name. A line starting with "Review:" names the source file to inspect where no automated test covers the requirement; such requirements also carry the comment "No automated test."
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Server lifecycle and options

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Start on an ephemeral loopback port
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpServer.Start()`` with no options (or null) shall start listening immediately on the IPv4 loopback address on an ephemeral port, exposing the bound address and port through ``Host`` and ``Port``, and ``ToString()`` shall return ``smtp://<Host>:<Port>``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- SmtpTests.the ready-made SMTP server captures the mail
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Configurable listening endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The server shall listen on ``SmtpServerOptions.Address`` and ``SmtpServerOptions.Port`` when they are set; a port of 0 (the default) shall select an ephemeral port.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Implicit TLS requires a certificate
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpServer.Start`` shall throw ``ArgumentException`` when ``ImplicitTls`` is true and ``Tls`` is null.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Implicit TLS from the first byte
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ImplicitTls`` is true, every connection shall complete a TLS handshake with the ``Tls`` certificate before the greeting is sent (port 465 style), STARTTLS shall not be advertised, and captured messages shall have ``Tls`` set to true.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TCP-level options pass through
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpServerOptions.Server`` (a ``ServerOptions``) shall configure the underlying ``TcpServer`` exposed as ``SmtpServer.Tcp``, including faults, concurrency, logging, transcripts and ``MaxLineLength``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.OverlongLine_GetsA500AndTheConnectionCloses_WithoutAHandlerError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stopping and disposing
STATEMENT: >>>
``StopAsync()`` shall stop accepting connections and close every open session, with the semantics of ``StreamServer.StopAsync``; ``DisposeAsync()`` shall dispose the underlying TCP server.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test. ``DisposeAsync`` is exercised by every test's ``await using`` but its effect is not asserted.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler errors are surfaced
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpServer.Errors`` shall expose the underlying TCP server's handler exceptions and ``ThrowIfFaulted()`` shall throw if any occurred; protocol errors by the client (malformed commands, disconnects, over-long lines) shall not be recorded as handler errors.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mail_SizeParameter_IsCheckedRobustly
- SmtpServerTests.ClientVanishingMidData_DeliversNothing
- SmtpProtocolTests.OverlongLine_GetsA500AndTheConnectionCloses_WithoutAHandlerError
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Greeting, EHLO and HELO

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Service greeting
STATEMENT: >>>
On each new connection the server shall send ``220 <Domain> ESMTP Intertube.Stub``, where ``Domain`` is ``SmtpServerOptions.Domain`` (default ``smtp.intertube.test``).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- SmtpTests.the ready-made SMTP server captures the mail
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The tests rely on a valid 220 greeting; none asserts its exact text.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EHLO multi-line reply
STATEMENT: >>>
``EHLO <domain>`` shall be answered with a multi-line 250 reply whose first line is ``250-<Domain> greets <domain>``, followed by one line per extension, every line but the last using ``250-`` and the last using ``250`` followed by a space.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Always-advertised extensions
STATEMENT: >>>
The EHLO reply shall always advertise, in this order, ``SIZE <MaxMessageSize>``, ``PIPELINING``, ``8BITMIME``, ``SMTPUTF8`` and ``ENHANCEDSTATUSCODES``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The test asserts only that ``ENHANCEDSTATUSCODES`` is the last line when neither TLS nor AUTH is configured.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: STARTTLS advertised only when available
STATEMENT: >>>
The EHLO reply shall advertise ``STARTTLS`` if and only if ``Tls`` is set and the connection is not already using TLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH advertised only when users are configured
STATEMENT: >>>
The EHLO reply shall advertise ``AUTH PLAIN LOGIN`` (after STARTTLS, if present) if and only if ``Users`` contains at least one account.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: HELO
STATEMENT: >>>
``HELO <domain>`` shall be answered with the single line ``250 <Domain>`` and shall mark the session as greeted, without advertising extensions.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.ClientVanishingMidData_DeliversNothing
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EHLO and HELO require a domain
STATEMENT: >>>
``EHLO`` or ``HELO`` without an argument shall be answered with ``501 5.5.4 Syntax: EHLO domain`` (or ``HELO domain``) and shall not mark the session as greeted.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Greeting_NeedsADomain
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EHLO and HELO reset the transaction
STATEMENT: >>>
A successful ``EHLO`` or ``HELO`` shall discard any mail transaction in progress (sender and recipients) and shall not change the authentication state.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Mail transaction

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MAIL requires a greeting
STATEMENT: >>>
``MAIL`` before a successful ``EHLO`` or ``HELO`` shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Say EHLO first``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MAIL FROM starts a transaction
STATEMENT: >>>
A valid ``MAIL FROM:<address>`` in a greeted session (and, where configured, over TLS and authenticated) shall be answered with ``250 2.1.0 OK`` and shall record the address, without angle brackets, as the transaction's sender.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- SmtpTests.the ready-made SMTP server captures the mail
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Null reverse path
STATEMENT: >>>
``MAIL FROM:<>`` shall be accepted, and the captured message's ``From`` shall be the empty string.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
RFC 5321 uses the null reverse path for bounces and other delivery notifications, which code under test may send.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Lenient path syntax
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``FROM:`` and ``TO:`` keywords shall be matched case-insensitively, whitespace after the colon shall be ignored, and an address without angle brackets shall be accepted up to the first space.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.FailNext_MatchesTheCanonicalFormOfTheCommand
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Malformed MAIL path
STATEMENT: >>>
``MAIL`` whose argument does not start with ``FROM:``, has no address, or has an unclosed ``<`` shall be answered with ``501 5.5.4 Syntax: MAIL FROM:<address>`` and shall not start a transaction.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mail_SizeParameter_IsCheckedRobustly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Nested MAIL refused
STATEMENT: >>>
``MAIL`` while a transaction is already in progress shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Nested MAIL command`` and shall leave the existing transaction unchanged.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SIZE parameter syntax
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``SIZE`` parameter (matched case-insensitively among the parameters after the path) whose value is empty or contains anything other than ASCII digits shall be answered with ``501 5.5.4 Syntax: SIZE=<number>``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mail_SizeParameter_IsCheckedRobustly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SIZE parameter over the limit
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``SIZE`` value greater than ``MaxMessageSize`` (default 10 MiB), including one too large to represent as a 64-bit integer, shall be answered with ``552 5.3.4 Message size exceeds fixed limit`` without an internal error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mail_SizeParameter_IsCheckedRobustly
- SmtpServerTests.OversizedMessage_IsRefusedUpFrontOrAfterData
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameters only after the path
STATEMENT: >>>
Text inside the angle-bracketed path shall not be interpreted as an ESMTP parameter; for example ``MAIL FROM:<SIZE=99999999999@x.test>`` shall be accepted.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mail_SizeParameter_IsCheckedRobustly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: RCPT TO adds a recipient
STATEMENT: >>>
A valid ``RCPT TO:<address>`` during a transaction shall be answered with ``250 2.1.5 OK`` and the address shall be appended to the transaction's recipients, so that every accepted recipient (including Bcc recipients not named in the headers) appears in ``SmtpMessage.Recipients`` in order.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: RCPT requires MAIL
STATEMENT: >>>
``RCPT`` outside a mail transaction shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Need MAIL first``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Malformed RCPT path
STATEMENT: >>>
``RCPT`` whose argument does not start with ``TO:``, or whose address is missing or empty (including ``<>``), shall be answered with ``501 5.5.4 Syntax: RCPT TO:<address>`` and shall not add a recipient.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DATA requires a recipient
STATEMENT: >>>
``DATA`` before any recipient has been accepted shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Need RCPT first``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DATA acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
``DATA`` with at least one recipient shall be answered with ``354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>``; once the message is complete and accepted it shall be captured and answered with ``250 2.0.0 OK: queued as <n>``, where n is the number of messages the server has captured.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
- SmtpProtocolTests.Data_OnlyCrLfDotCrLfEndsTheMessage_AndLineEndingsAreKept
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Only CRLF.CRLF ends the data
STATEMENT: >>>
The message data shall end only at a line consisting of a single ``.`` that both follows a CRLF and is terminated by CRLF; a ``.`` line ended by a bare LF, or following a line ended by a bare LF, shall be treated as message content.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Accepting looser terminators would let a client smuggle a second message past a stricter relay (SMTP smuggling).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Data_OnlyCrLfDotCrLfEndsTheMessage_AndLineEndingsAreKept
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dot-unstuffing
STATEMENT: >>>
A leading ``.`` on a data line that starts after a CRLF shall be removed before the line is stored (RFC 5321 section 4.5.2).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Data stored verbatim
STATEMENT: >>>
Apart from dot-unstuffing and the removal of the terminating ``.`` line, ``SmtpMessage.Data`` shall hold the message bytes exactly as sent, without normalising line endings.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Data_OnlyCrLfDotCrLfEndsTheMessage_AndLineEndingsAreKept
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oversized data refused after transfer
STATEMENT: >>>
When the received data exceeds ``MaxMessageSize``, the server shall read it to the end-of-data marker, answer ``552 5.3.4 Message size exceeds fixed limit``, capture nothing and end the transaction; data beyond the limit shall not be buffered.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.OversizedMessage_IsRefusedUpFrontOrAfterData
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-034
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Disconnect during data delivers nothing
STATEMENT: >>>
If the client disconnects before the end-of-data marker, no message shall be captured and no handler error shall be recorded.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.ClientVanishingMidData_DeliversNothing
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-035
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Transaction ends after data
STATEMENT: >>>
After the end-of-data marker the transaction shall be reset whatever the outcome (accepted, too large or refused by an injected reply), so the client may start a new transaction with ``MAIL`` on the same connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-036
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pipelined commands
STATEMENT: >>>
Commands sent together without waiting for replies (PIPELINING, RFC 2920) shall each be answered in order.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.DotStuffing_IsUndone_AndPipelinedCommandsAreAnswered
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Other commands

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-037
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Verbs are case-insensitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The command verb (the first space-separated word of the line) shall be matched case-insensitively.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.FailNext_MatchesTheCanonicalFormOfTheCommand
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-038
STATUS: Active
TITLE: RSET
STATEMENT: >>>
``RSET`` shall discard any mail transaction in progress and be answered with ``250 2.0.0 OK``, without changing the greeting or authentication state.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-039
STATUS: Active
TITLE: NOOP
STATEMENT: >>>
``NOOP`` shall be answered with ``250 2.0.0 OK`` without changing any state.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-040
STATUS: Active
TITLE: VRFY and HELP
STATEMENT: >>>
``VRFY`` shall be answered with ``252 2.1.5 Cannot verify, but will accept`` and ``HELP`` with ``214 2.0.0 See RFC 5321``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-041
STATUS: Active
TITLE: QUIT
STATEMENT: >>>
``QUIT`` shall be answered with ``221 2.0.0 Bye`` and the server shall then close the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test. The BCL and MailKit clients in the tests send QUIT, but no test asserts the reply or the close.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-042
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unknown commands
STATEMENT: >>>
Any unrecognised command shall be answered with ``500 5.5.1 Command not recognised`` and the session shall continue.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-043
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Over-long lines close the connection
STATEMENT: >>>
A command or data line longer than ``ServerOptions.MaxLineLength`` shall cause the server to record the transcript event ``line too long``, reply ``500 5.5.2 Line too long`` and close the connection, without recording a handler error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.OverlongLine_GetsA500AndTheConnectionCloses_WithoutAHandlerError
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The test covers a command line; the same limit applies to lines inside DATA.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: STARTTLS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-044
STATUS: Active
TITLE: STARTTLS unavailable
STATEMENT: >>>
``STARTTLS`` shall be answered with ``502 5.5.1 STARTTLS not available`` when ``Tls`` is not set or the connection already uses TLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-045
STATUS: Active
TITLE: STARTTLS takes no argument
STATEMENT: >>>
``STARTTLS`` with an argument shall be answered with ``501 5.5.4 Syntax: STARTTLS`` and shall not start TLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-046
STATUS: Active
TITLE: STARTTLS upgrade resets the session
STATEMENT: >>>
A valid ``STARTTLS`` shall be answered with ``220 2.0.0 Ready to start TLS``, followed by a TLS handshake with the ``Tls`` certificate; afterwards the session shall forget the greeting, any transaction and any authentication (RFC 3207 section 4.2), so the client must send ``EHLO`` again, and the new EHLO reply shall not advertise STARTTLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Input pipelined after STARTTLS is refused
STATEMENT: >>>
If any input is already buffered after the ``STARTTLS`` line, the server shall record the transcript event ``commands pipelined after STARTTLS``, reply ``554 5.5.0 Improper command pipelining after STARTTLS`` and close the connection without starting TLS.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Commands injected in plaintext behind STARTTLS would otherwise be processed as if they had arrived over TLS (CVE-2011-0411).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.StartTls_WithPipelinedCommands_IsRefusedAndClosed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: RequireTls enforcement
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``RequireTls`` is true, ``MAIL`` on a connection not using TLS shall be answered with ``530 5.7.0 Must issue a STARTTLS command first``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
``RequireTls`` without ``Tls`` (and without ``ImplicitTls``) is accepted by ``Start`` but makes every ``MAIL`` fail, since TLS can never be established.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Authentication

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-049
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH disabled without users
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``Users`` is null or empty, ``AUTH`` shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Authentication not enabled`` and ``MAIL`` shall not require authentication.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-050
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MAIL requires authentication
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``Users`` contains at least one account, ``MAIL`` before a successful ``AUTH`` shall be answered with ``530 5.7.0 Authentication required``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH PLAIN
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH PLAIN`` shall take the base64 response either as an initial response on the command line or after an empty ``334`` challenge, decode it as UTF-8 ``authzid NUL user NUL password``, and answer ``235 2.7.0 Authentication successful`` when the user and password match an entry in ``Users``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Auth_FollowsRfc4954
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The authorization identity is ignored. The empty-challenge form is not covered by a test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-052
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH LOGIN
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH LOGIN`` shall prompt for the user name with ``334 VXNlcm5hbWU6`` (unless given as an initial response) and for the password with ``334 UGFzc3dvcmQ6``, each response being base64 UTF-8, and answer ``235 2.7.0 Authentication successful`` when they match an entry in ``Users``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-053
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Invalid credentials
STATEMENT: >>>
Credentials that do not match ``Users`` (or a PLAIN response without exactly three NUL-separated fields) shall be answered with ``535 5.7.8 Authentication credentials invalid`` and the session shall remain unauthenticated.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
- OrderNotifierTests.WrongPassword_FailsWithoutSendingCredentialsInTheClear
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-054
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unknown mechanism
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH`` with a mechanism other than PLAIN or LOGIN (matched case-insensitively), or with none, shall be answered with ``504 5.5.4 Unrecognised authentication type``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-055
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH only after EHLO
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH`` before a successful ``EHLO`` or ``HELO`` shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Say EHLO first`` (RFC 4954 section 4).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Auth_FollowsRfc4954
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-056
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No AUTH during a transaction
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH`` while a mail transaction is in progress shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 AUTH not permitted during a mail transaction``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test. In practice this is reachable only when the transaction began before authentication was required, which cannot happen while ``Users`` is set; the check is defensive.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-057
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH only once
STATEMENT: >>>
``AUTH`` after a successful authentication shall be answered with ``503 5.5.1 Already authenticated``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-058
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Cancelling an exchange
STATEMENT: >>>
A response of ``*`` to a 334 challenge shall cancel the exchange with ``501 5.7.0 Authentication cancelled``, leave the session unauthenticated, and record the transcript message ``AUTH <mechanism> cancelled``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Auth_FollowsRfc4954
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-059
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Empty SASL response
STATEMENT: >>>
A SASL response of ``=`` shall be treated as an empty string (RFC 4954 section 4).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-060
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Undecodable SASL response
STATEMENT: >>>
A SASL response that is not valid base64 shall end the exchange with ``501 5.5.2 Cannot decode response`` and record the transcript message ``AUTH <mechanism> malformed response``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Auth_FollowsRfc4954
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-061
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Disconnect during AUTH
STATEMENT: >>>
If the client disconnects while the server awaits a SASL response, the server shall record the transcript message ``AUTH <mechanism> aborted: connection closed`` and end the session without a handler error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-062
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AUTH outcome in the transcript
STATEMENT: >>>
Each completed AUTH exchange shall record the received transcript message ``AUTH <mechanism> user=<user> accepted`` or ``AUTH <mechanism> user=<user> rejected``, and never the password.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Auth_PlainAndLogin_AndMailRequiresIt
- OrderNotifierTests.WrongPassword_FailsWithoutSendingCredentialsInTheClear
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The raw base64 responses still appear in the transcript as received lines; only the summary message omits the password.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-063
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Authenticated user on the message
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpMessage.User`` shall be the user name the session authenticated as, or null if it did not authenticate.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Fault injection and interception

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-064
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FailNext
STATEMENT: >>>
``FailNext(command, reply, times)`` shall answer the next ``times`` (default 1) commands matching the ``LineMatcher`` with ``reply`` instead of handling them, and then stop matching; ``times`` less than 1 shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.FailNext_Greylisting_ThenTheRetryIsDelivered
- OrderNotifierTests.Greylisting_IsRetried_AndDeliversExactlyOnce
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-065
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FailAlways
STATEMENT: >>>
``FailAlways(command, reply)`` shall answer every matching command with ``reply`` for the lifetime of the server.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.FailAlways_RejectsOneDomain_AndEndOfDataCanBeRefused
- OrderNotifierTests.PermanentRejection_IsNotRetried
- SmtpTests.a rejected recipient surfaces as SmtpFailedRecipientException
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-066
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Matching the canonical command form
STATEMENT: >>>
A rule shall match if its pattern matches either the command line as sent or its canonical form, in which the verb is upper-cased and, for ``MAIL`` and ``RCPT``, the keyword before the colon is upper-cased with surrounding whitespace removed and no space follows the colon; so ``RCPT TO:<a@b>`` also matches ``rcpt to: <a@b>``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.FailNext_MatchesTheCanonicalFormOfTheCommand
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-067
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Refusing a message at end of data
STATEMENT: >>>
A rule or interceptor matching the end-of-data command ``.`` shall be applied after the data has been received; its reply shall replace the 250 acceptance and the message shall not be captured.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.FailAlways_RejectsOneDomain_AndEndOfDataCanBeRefused
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
An oversized message is refused with 552 before any ``.`` rule is consulted, so such a rule is not consumed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-068
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Injected replies leave state unchanged
STATEMENT: >>>
When a rule or interceptor supplies a reply, the command shall not be processed: the session state shall not change, so for example an injected 250 to ``MAIL`` does not start a transaction and a refused ``RCPT`` does not add a recipient.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.FailAlways_RejectsOneDomain_AndEndOfDataCanBeRefused
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The test covers the end-of-data case (nothing captured); state retention for MAIL and RCPT is not asserted directly.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-069
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rule precedence
STATEMENT: >>>
Rules shall be consulted in the order they were added, the first matching rule with uses remaining supplying the reply, and ``Intercept`` shall be called only when no rule matched.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-070
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Intercept hook
STATEMENT: >>>
``Intercept``, when set, shall be called with an ``SmtpCommand`` (the full ``Line``, the upper-cased ``Verb`` and the ``Connection``; for end of data the line and verb ``.`` and the received ``Message``) before each command is handled; a non-null result shall be sent as the reply instead of handling the command, and null shall let the server proceed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Intercept_421_ClosesTheConnection
- OrderNotifierTests.ConnectionDroppedBeforeTheServerAccepted_IsRetried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-071
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Injected 421 closes the connection
STATEMENT: >>>
After sending an injected reply starting with ``421`` (from a rule or ``Intercept``) the server shall close the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.Intercept_421_ClosesTheConnection
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-072
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connection ended by an interceptor
STATEMENT: >>>
If the connection has been terminated (for example by ``Connection.Abort()`` in ``Intercept``) when the hook returns, the server shall send nothing further, end the session and, for end of data, not capture the message.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- OrderNotifierTests.ConnectionDroppedBeforeTheServerAccepted_IsRetried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-073
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Hooks see commands only
STATEMENT: >>>
Rules and ``Intercept`` shall be applied to command lines and to the end-of-data command, but not to individual message data lines or to SASL responses during an AUTH exchange.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpSession.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Captured messages and transcripts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-074
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Captured messages in order
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpServer.Messages`` shall return a snapshot of every accepted message, from all connections, in the order they were accepted.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- SmtpServerTests.FailNext_Greylisting_ThenTheRetryIsDelivered
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-075
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Envelope on the message
STATEMENT: >>>
Each ``SmtpMessage`` shall carry the envelope sender ``From``, the accepted ``Recipients``, the raw ``Data``, the authenticated ``User``, whether it arrived over TLS (``Tls``), the ``ConnectionId`` used in the transcript, and the UTC time of acceptance ``ReceivedAt``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-076
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Message text and summary
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpMessage.Text`` shall be ``Data`` decoded as UTF-8, and ``ToString()`` shall return ``<From> -> <recipients joined by ", ">: <Subject>``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Data_OnlyCrLfDotCrLfEndsTheMessage_AndLineEndingsAreKept
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_MalformedEncodingsAreLeftAsSent_NeverThrown
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-077
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Waiting for a matching message
STATEMENT: >>>
``WaitForMessageAsync(predicate, timeout, cancellationToken)`` shall complete with the first captured message matching ``predicate`` (any message when null), whether it arrived before or during the call, and shall throw ``TimeoutException`` after ``timeout`` (default 5 seconds) with a description listing the messages received.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.WaitForMessage_ReturnsTheMatchingMail
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The timeout path is not tested.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-078
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Waiting for a message count
STATEMENT: >>>
``WaitForMessagesAsync(count, timeout, cancellationToken)`` shall complete once at least ``count`` messages have been captured and throw ``TimeoutException`` if that does not happen within ``timeout`` (default 5 seconds).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpServer.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-079
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Accepted message in the transcript
STATEMENT: >>>
Each captured message shall be recorded in the connection's transcript as the received message ``MESSAGE <From> -> <recipients>: <Subject>``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SMTP-080
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Plaintext transcript after STARTTLS
STATEMENT: >>>
The transcript of ``SmtpServer.Tcp`` shall record the dialogue in plaintext both before and after STARTTLS, including message content.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
- OrderNotifierTests.WrongPassword_FailsWithoutSendingCredentialsInTheClear
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: MIME reading of captured messages

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Header fields in order, unfolded
STATEMENT: >>>
``SmtpMessage.Headers`` shall list the header fields of the top-level entity in order, each name trimmed, each value unfolded by removing the CRLF before a continuation line while keeping its leading whitespace, and trimmed at both ends.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_FoldedHeaderKeepsItsWhitespace_AndEncodedWordsDecode
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Only CRLF is recognised as a line break in the header section; a message using bare LF line endings has no recognised header/body separator, so its whole content is read as headers.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Header lookup
STATEMENT: >>>
``Header(name)`` shall return the value of the first header field with that name, compared case-insensitively, or null if there is none; ``Subject`` shall equal ``Header("Subject")``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_FoldedHeaderKeepsItsWhitespace_AndEncodedWordsDecode
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: RFC 2047 encoded words
STATEMENT: >>>
Encoded words of the form ``=?charset?B?text?=`` and ``=?charset?Q?text?=`` in header values shall be decoded in their charset (with ``_`` meaning space in Q encoding), and whitespace between two adjacent encoded words shall be removed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_FoldedHeaderKeepsItsWhitespace_AndEncodedWordsDecode
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Malformed encoded words left as sent
STATEMENT: >>>
An encoded word whose charset is unknown or whose B-encoded text is not valid base64 shall be left exactly as sent (RFC 2047 section 6.3).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_MalformedEncodingsAreLeftAsSent_NeverThrown
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Raw 8-bit header values
STATEMENT: >>>
A header value containing raw 8-bit bytes shall be decoded as UTF-8 when the bytes are valid UTF-8 (as sent with SMTPUTF8), and otherwise kept byte for byte as Latin-1 characters.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpMessage.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charsets without global registration
STATEMENT: >>>
Charset names in encoded words and ``Content-Type`` parameters shall be resolved to the built-in .NET encodings and also to the Windows and ISO code pages of ``CodePagesEncodingProvider``, without registering that provider process-wide; surrounding quotes and whitespace in the name shall be ignored.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Registering an encoding provider changes ``Encoding.GetEncoding`` for the whole test process, which a test double must not do.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_EightBitBodyIsDecodedInItsDeclaredCharset
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_FoldedHeaderKeepsItsWhitespace_AndEncodedWordsDecode
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The tests decode windows-1252 and iso-8859-1; that the provider is not registered globally is not asserted.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Body charset
STATEMENT: >>>
A text body shall be decoded in the charset named by the ``charset`` parameter of its ``Content-Type``, or as UTF-8 when the parameter is absent or names an unknown charset.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_EightBitBodyIsDecodedInItsDeclaredCharset
- SmtpServerTests.BclSmtpClient_MessageIsCaptured_WithDecodedSubjectAndBody
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Quoted-printable bodies
STATEMENT: >>>
A body with ``Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable`` shall be decoded, with ``=XX`` hex escapes turned into bytes and soft line breaks (``=`` at the end of a line) removed, before charset decoding.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_TextBodySkipsAttachments_AndSearchesNestedParts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Base64 bodies
STATEMENT: >>>
A body with ``Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64`` shall be decoded ignoring whitespace and tolerating missing padding; a body that is not valid base64 shall be left as sent.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_MalformedEncodingsAreLeftAsSent_NeverThrown
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The test covers invalid base64 left as sent; successful base64 decoding is exercised only indirectly by clients that choose base64.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Other transfer encodings
STATEMENT: >>>
A body with no ``Content-Transfer-Encoding`` or any other value (such as ``7bit`` or ``8bit``) shall be taken byte for byte and decoded only by its charset.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_EightBitBodyIsDecodedInItsDeclaredCharset
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Multipart boundaries per RFC 2046
STATEMENT: >>>
An entity whose ``Content-Type`` is ``multipart/*`` with a non-empty ``boundary`` parameter (quoted or not) shall be split into parts at delimiter lines, ``--boundary`` preceded by CRLF (or at the start of the body); the preamble before the first delimiter and everything after the closing ``--boundary--`` shall be ignored, and boundary text that does not begin a line shall be treated as content.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_TextBodySkipsAttachments_AndSearchesNestedParts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parts without headers
STATEMENT: >>>
A body part that begins with a blank line shall be treated as having no header fields, and therefore as ``text/plain`` (RFC 2046 section 5.1.1).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpMessage.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Default content type
STATEMENT: >>>
An entity without a ``Content-Type`` header shall be treated as ``text/plain``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_MalformedEncodingsAreLeftAsSent_NeverThrown
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TextBody selects the first plain-text part
STATEMENT: >>>
``TextBody`` shall return the decoded body of the first ``text/plain`` entity that is not an attachment (``Content-Disposition`` starting with ``attachment``), searching nested multipart entities depth-first in order; for a non-multipart message this is its own decoded body.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_TextBodySkipsAttachments_AndSearchesNestedParts
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
- SmtpTests.the ready-made SMTP server captures the mail
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TextBody fallback
STATEMENT: >>>
When no suitable ``text/plain`` part exists, ``TextBody`` shall return the decoded body of the first leaf part, or the empty string if there is none.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Smtp/SmtpMessage.cs
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-MIME-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MIME reading never throws
STATEMENT: >>>
Reading ``Headers``, ``Header``, ``Subject``, ``TextBody`` or ``ToString()`` shall never throw because of malformed message content; anything that cannot be decoded shall be returned as it was sent, and ``Data`` shall be unaffected.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.Mime_MalformedEncodingsAreLeftAsSent_NeverThrown
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
